/- Universal original-source right-coset checking assembled from exact finite intervals.
The actual subgroup is the fixed subgroup of terminal substitution. Its ten supplied symbols
are the nine original nonterminal C422 vertices and the proved redundant longest symbol F1.
Original f1 is omitted from those inputs. Every other input equation is an actual source
square, Coxeter/spider consequence, proved longest-word consequence, or acyclic path definition.
The 10296 chronological claims are interpreted through the original-source right-coset checker.
The final literal claim states f1 times the inverse identity belongs to this actual subgroup. -/
